{%- comment -%}
  Product card — every value one of the product's options carries.

  "18K, 22K". The words around it are not here: this block renders the list and
  a `product-card-text` beside it in a `group` says "Available in", which is the
  same composition the caption uses. A shop that wants "Comes in", "Sizes:" or
  nothing at all types it there rather than asking the theme for a setting.

  **The option is named by the merchant, and matched rather than positioned.** A
  text setting — "Karat", "Size", "Length" — matched case-insensitively against
  each option's name. Position would be simpler and is wrong on a mixed
  catalogue: one product ordered Metal, Karat and another Karat, Metal cannot
  both be served by "the second option". A name finds the right one either way,
  and renders nothing on a product with no such option, which is the honest
  answer for a catalogue where only some pieces carry it.

  **The order is the merchant's own.** The block before this sorted numerically
  — pulling the first number out of each value and zero-padding it so "9K"
  sorted before "22K". That is right for karats and arbitrary for everything
  else: "Brushed, Polished" has no number, and S/M/L/XL sorts wrongly under
  every rule except the one the merchant already applied in admin.

  **Every value is listed, whatever the stock.** An option value exists because
  the piece can be made that way, so a sold-out one is still something the shop
  offers; filtering on `available` would make the sentence flicker as inventory
  moved.

  Its style and element controls are `product-card-text`'s, from the same
  `snippets/text-style.liquid` — a merchant setting one half of a row should not
  find the other half cannot be set the same way.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product = block.settings.product | default: closest.product
  assign wanted = block.settings.option_name | downcase | strip

  assign values_option = blank
  if wanted != blank
    for option in product.options_with_values
      assign option_down = option.name | downcase
      if option_down contains wanted
        assign values_option = option
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  assign separator = block.settings.separator | default: ', '

  assign values_list = ''
  if values_option != blank
    for value in values_option.values
      if forloop.first
        assign values_list = value | append: ''
      else
        assign values_list = values_list | append: separator | append: value
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  assign tags = 'span,p,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6' | split: ','
  assign tag = 'span'
  if tags contains block.settings.element
    assign tag = block.settings.element
  endif
-%}

{%- if values_list != blank -%}
  <{{ tag }}
    class="card__meta card__text"
    style="{% render 'text-style', preset: block.settings.style, font_style: block.settings.override_font, font_size: block.settings.override_size, color: block.settings.color, line_height: block.settings.override_leading, text_case: block.settings.override_case, letter_spacing: block.settings.override_tracking %}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >{{ values_list }}</{{ tag }}>
{%- endif -%}

